{
  "$comment": "How a genius is assembled: its body (one per silhouette) and parts (one per feature) on named sockets. When the art exists, the body is game/assets/genius/bodies/<silhouette>.glb with empties named socket_<name>, and each part is game/assets/genius/parts/<feature>.glb; the game uses them and ignores the placeholders below. Placeholder bodies are built from a kind: quadruped and humanoid kinds borrow a rigged model, so they walk; the rest are shapes. Socket positions are in metres on the placeholder before it is scaled to the genius's height; 'bone' sockets ride the rig. featureSockets names the sockets some features use instead of their slot's (a beak and fangs at the mouth, small hands at the wrists, a brush in the grip, a tail at the tail's root); a body without those sockets falls back to the slot's. A part hung on a right-hand socket (a name ending in _r, fr or br) is mirrored: parts of a pair are made for the left. artSize is how tall a silhouette's art body stands against its instar's size (default 1): an art body carries its own proportions, so scale applies only to the placeholder. carries lists features a silhouette's art body already wears in its own design (the stag its antlers), so no part is hung for them. A surface feature hangs nothing unless it has a part and is named in featureSockets (the Seed-marks a grip and a ledger: a handle on its back, a book at its chest). How one genius differs from another of its form (coat, markings, build, keepsake) is in genius-looks.json.",
